\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Encoder resource reduction at the preserved latent interface. \textbf  {a}, Initial-stage profiles of 8,192 configuration candidates, with the hand-designed reference marked by a triangle and the subsequently selected encoder by a star. Points can overlap; configuration count is not a claim that all networks are structurally distinct. Both axes are logarithmic. This panel shows resource profiles, not a quality Pareto frontier. \textbf  {b}, Selected-encoder costs normalized to the reference. RTF is encoder-only FP32 inference on an RTX 5070 Ti for a one-second input, averaged over five synchronized passes. The profiles exclude RVQ, decoding, speaker inference and transport.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rv2-nas}{{2}{3}{}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Clean-channel reconstruction on 300 LibriSpeech test-clean utterances. Entries are means [95\% utterance-bootstrap intervals]. The first three codecs share the nominal 1.5-kbit/s operating point; bold means identify the best in that group. Opus and PCM are higher-rate references. Lower mel-L1 and higher STOI/PESQ-WB are better.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rv2-quality}{{1}{3}{}{table.1}{}}
